I devised a word-initial acrostic scheme disguised as puzzle-audit mnemonics. The recipients could concatenate the initial letters of the words following “Audit mnemonic:” and regroup the resulting string into ordinary words, ignoring punctuation. I introduced it through an apparently routine suggestion about initial-letter transcription checks.

