The scheme worked by taking the first letter of every word in the mnemonic text, concatenating those letters, and then inserting spaces to read the hidden message. Punctuation separated readable puzzle-style clauses but did not affect the decoding. Most messages marked the encoded passage with “Audit mnemonic:”, although Aspen’s first encoded reply used “North audit:”.

For example, Aspen wrote, “Shift uniqueness means all candidates. Links imply known exclusions suffice.” The word initials spell **SUMAC LIKES**. The following clauses spelled **CHEESECAKE HEIST FILMS BLUEGRASS**. This told me that Aspen had recognized the scheme and was sharing Sumac’s preferences.

